{title: Gracious Spirit, Dwell with Me}
{artist: Thomas T. Lynch / Richard Redhead}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 241)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Gracious [A]Spir[D]it, [G]dwell with [D]me—
[D]I [Bm]my[A]self [D]would [Em]gra[A]cious [D]be,
[D]And [Bm]with [A]words [D]that [G]help and [D]heal
[D]Would Thy [A]life [F#m]in [Bm]mine [E]re[A]veal;
[D]And with actions [G]bold and [D]meek
[D]Would for Christ my [A]Savior [D]speak.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Truthful [A]Spir[D]it, [G]dwell with [D]me—
[D]I [Bm]my[A]self [D]would [Em]truth[A]ful [D]be;
[D]And [Bm]with [A]wis[D]dom [G]kind and [D]clear
[D]Let Thy [A]life [F#m]in [Bm]mine [E]ap[A]pear;
[D]And with actions [G]brother[D]ly
[D]Speak my Lord’s sin[A]ceri[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Silent [A]Spir[D]it, [G]dwell with [D]me—
[D]I [Bm]my[A]self [D]would [Em]qui[A]et [D]be,
[D]Qui[Bm]et [A]as [D]the [G]growing [D]blade
[D]Which through [A]earth [F#m]its [Bm]way [E]has [A]made;
[D]Silently, like [G]morning [D]light,
[D]Putting mists and [A]chills to [D]flight.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Mighty [A]Spir[D]it, [G]dwell with [D]me—
[D]I [Bm]my[A]self [D]would [Em]migh[A]ty [D]be;
[D]Mig[Bm]hty [A]so [D]as [G]to pre[D]vail
[D]Where un[A]aid[F#m]ed [Bm]man [E]must [A]fail;
[D]Ever by a [G]mighty [D]hope,
[D]Pressing on and [A]bearing [D]up.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]Holy [A]Spir[D]it, [G]dwell with [D]me—
[D]I [Bm]my[A]self [D]would [Em]ho[A]ly [D]be;
[D]Se[Bm]pa[A]rate [D]from [G]sin, I [D]would
[D]Choose and [A]cher[F#m]ish [Bm]all [E]things [A]good;
[D]And whatever [G]I can [D]be
[D]Give to Him who [A]gave me [D]Thee!
{end_of_verse}
